    "summary": "Turn 47 delivered the map handoff for the two most recent confirmed results, so the understanding layer carries both mechanisms.\n\nState on entry. Seven claims are settled, six of them confirmed in scope (C1 recovery divergence, C2 stable-store record, C3 applied-state divergence, C4 the NOOP-commit crash, C6 the promoted-leader variant, and C7 pending this handoff's context) plus C5 as a bounded no-violation protection. The two most recent increment sources are the promoted-leader variant (claim C6, artifact f2523a67a7e94950b0eacff7c280a42a) and the dead accept-rejection path (claim C7, artifact 374c3ca1233e4a00af8a1f18626ea9db).\n\nMap update (accepted base version 9, two clarified objects). Behavior B5-slow-path-accept gained a branch recording that the ballot-equality gate returns before the nack branch, so a higher-ballot AcceptReply is never counted as a rejection — with the confirmed observation (nacks 0, accept_oks 0, no reaction) and a residual unknown that the timeout-driven recovery and the multi-reply case were not exercised. core_overview's context explanation now records that the same masking holds for the deployment's promoted replica (IsLeader true, with the ballot raised past maxRecvBallot), citing claim C6, and a new open detail states the dead rejection path together with the absence of any pre-accept rejection signal, since PreAcceptReply copies the request's ballot and handlePreAccept returns silently for a smaller one — leaving progress after a rejection to the 10s execution timeout. Both changes carry map_changes entries with sources and preserves explanations, so no requirement, binding, edge, identity or fact context moved.\n\nRemaining, recorded rather than absorbed: the timeout-driven recovery path is not exercised by any check, so the delay's real length in a deployment is unmeasured; the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact; and the unread helper surfaces (replica/sender.go, replica/mset.go, hook/). No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
